  "checked_conclusions": [
    "Original finite dyadic upper-carry layers equal the moving high-digit central-binomial parity code; every prefix is bounded by H=2^k.",
    "Exact unit-cell power response, not quadrature: prefix bound B gives source-normalized norm <=2B/X for beta<=1, X>0.",
    "Every moving highCode packet with H/X->0 loses the diagnostic matched power source, uniformly in its other interval endpoint.",
    "At X=H the normalized power response equals -(2^beta-1)/beta<0 for beta>0, while the arbitrary-weight arithmetic packet equals the negative original uncoded interval.",
    "The bounded correlated selector (1+code)/2 restores half the uncoded channel; no arbitrary-mask estimate follows.",
    "Actual native physicalRowWeight and spectralSummand with all powers and masks give an exact lossless border determinant equal to their original finite signed join.",
    "Bare determinant norm is invariant under actual supported spectral Mobius column signs; this alone supplies no prescribed-vector estimate."
  ],
  "paper_level_only": [
    "Mixed high-binary/low-ternary power-source deletion and blockwise published prime-theorem rate mismatch.",
    "General centered-prefix integration-by-parts principle and its sharp coarse two-cell countercheck.",
    "Whole-border common-integrality/Frobenius obligations and adjugate-source mismatch beyond the checked finite native border identity."
  ],
